# Routing for the direct-upload Pages project (#223).
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads routing from `_redirects` in the uploaded directory; a
# `[[redirects]]` table in wrangler.toml is never installed by
# `wrangler pages deploy`.
#
# The old `/*  /index.html  200` catch-all made every path a 200 shell: a
# curl-only agent could not tell a real page from a typo, and `/keys/zzz` served
# the app's own markup (#223). Only the routes below and the files in `dist/`
# answer now; everything else reaches 404.html.
#
# Do NOT add a 200 rewrite whose destination ends in `/index.html`: Pages
# normalises the destination to the clean URL, which then matches the rule
# again — wrangler rejects it as an infinite loop, and the served response is a
# 308 instead of the 200 the rule promises. The door pages are flat files
# (`dist/tokens.html`, `dist/keys.html`, `dist/sign-in.html`) which Pages
# already serves at `/tokens`, `/keys` and `/sign-in` with a 200, so they need
# no rule at all.

# Aliases — neither is a page of this app; kept so old links do not dead-end.
/overview      /mcp      301
/auth/sign-in  /sign-in  301

# The SPA's remaining routes are the same document as `/`; the clean URL
# `/tokens` etc. is a file, not a rewrite.
/mcp           /         200
/data          /         200

# Pages already strips the trailing slash on the three file-backed door routes
# with a 308; give the two proxied routes the same courtesy instead of a 404.
/mcp/          /mcp      301
/data/         /data     301
